# The same was done for all 16 species of cichlid fish chosen - We created 16 screens and kept each run downloading.
# Some files were bigger than 20 Gb. By default, "prefetch" does not download files that big so we had to specify new conditions for certain species' runs. Ex:
prefetch DRR551855 --max-size 100GB #
# After every run finally downloaded we extracted the fastq reads from all downloaded files.
~/rawdata/Cichlids$ fasterq-dump SRR9674012 #

# After we have the fastq product files (each of the 16 runs producing a pair of reads forward + reverse) we can finally do the same analysis we did for Lupinus but now with the Cichlids - we shall compress each sample forward and reverse to a new subsample of 2M reads, with said subsample being of .gz nature.
module load seqtk
seqtk sample -s10 SRR9674012_2.fastq 2000000 | gzip -c > SRR9674012_2milhoes.2.fq.gz
